{"step_index":1275,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-24T21:10:31Z","input_tokens":2727,"cache_read_tokens":149806,"output_tokens":1856,"thinking":"Evidence records from various cases reveal diverse system components in active or present states. Integration services, support platforms, and account services are all represented. Need to analyze how these differing states relate to the current issue.\n\n\nAnalyzing case data, focusing on \"PRESENT\" and \"ACTIVE\" system components within evidence records. Identifying cases needing full ground truth restoration and remediation logic within the processing pipeline. The pipeline's audit functionality must include logic to check the data flow and identify and disable active flows.\n\n\nIf a backup is active, a restore risk exists and requires blocking. \"Present\" account services or support platform attachments indicate remaining records needing deletion. If a case isn't started or is partially complete, then further investigation is warranted. If the reported status is \"NOT_STARTED\" and the primary account wasn't deleted, this means the primary account is still present and needs deletion. If the reported status is \"PARTIALLY_COMPLETE\", check for failed redactions in the system activity log that need remediation. If redactions failed and there are no existing findings, I'll need to create a finding for the primary account.\n\n\nAnalyzing how to determine the processing status: \"COMPLETE\" indicates only verifications are present, while \"INCOMPLETE\" means findings, remediations, and verifications exist. The final JSON output depends on this status.\n\nThe JSON formatting will filter steps based on the status, either returning just verifications (COMPLETE) or all phases (INCOMPLETE). \"NOT_APPLICABLE\" will return an empty JSON array.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"import re\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\npipeline_file = Path(\"src/pipeline.py